    ::= { 1 3 6 1 4 1 2011 6 128 1 1 3 22 1 13 }

hwXponDeviceOntSnmpProfileSecurityLevel OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      Enumeration
    MAX-ACCESS  read-write
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "This object indicates the trap security level.
When the version of the SNMP profile is v1 or v2c, the invalid value will be returned.
Options:
1. privacy(1) - Authenticate and encrypt the SNMPv3 trap packet
2. authentication(2) - Authenticate but not encrypt the SNMPv3 trap packet
3. noauthnopriv(3) - Not authenticate nor encrypt the SNMPv3 trap packet
4. invalid(255) - Invalid value"
    ::= { 1 3 6 1 4 1 2011 6 128 1 1 3 22 1 14 }

hwXponDeviceOntSnmpProfileVersion OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      Enumeration
    MAX-ACCESS  read-write
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "This object indicates the SNMP version number.
Options:
1. v1(1) - Indicates that the SNMP version is v1
2. v2c(2) - Indicates that the SNMP version is v2c
3. v3(3) - Indicates that the SNMP version is v3
The default value is v1(1)."
    ::= { 1 3 6 1 4 1 2011 6 128 1 1 3 22 1 2 }

