hwGponDeviceSrvProfPortVlanCfgPortCVlan OBJECT-TYPE
    SYNTAX      Integer32
    MAX-ACCESS  unknown
    STATUS      current
    DESCRIPTION
        "This object indicates the user-side VLAN of port on the GPON service profile.
Options:
1.user-vlan(0~4095) - Indicates the VLAN for user-side packets of an ONT port
2.transparent(65534) - Indicates the transparent transmission mode for packet forwarding. In this mode, packets are not processed and VLAN tags remain the same
3.untagged(65533) - Indicates that user-side packets before VLAN translation do not carry VLAN tags
4.other-all(65532) - Indicates that user-side packets before VLAN translation are ones that cannot be matched by specified VLAN or untagged VLAN
5.invalid(-1) - Indicates that there is no VLAN translation, or this port is not in VLAN translation mode, for example, user-side packets is in priority translation mode, not concerned VLAN ID."
